& [SolutionIdentity] is the completed shared-generation Codex tool surface
  + [solution_uuid] is ce25a800-4404-4ddb-98c0-5e272443eebb
  + [status] is completed_and_boundedly_activated
  + [tool] is query_sop
  + [startup_modes] is embedded and resident

& [PinnedServiceClient] is reusable loopback transport state
  + [construction] is ServiceClient::from_config
  + [snapshot] is validated endpoint, frame bound, timeouts, and redacted capability
  + [send] is one strict service request and identity-checked response
  + [compatibility] is send_request remains a one-invocation convenience wrapper
  + [security] is Debug redacts the token and running clients do not reread changed configuration

& [MCPBackend] is explicit
  + [embedded] is Arc PreparedRuntime from --environment
  + [resident] is Arc ServiceClient from --service-config
  + [startup] is authenticated Status before MCP STDIO begins
  + [environment_accessor] and [runtime_accessor] return none in resident mode rather than panic or imply ownership
  + [tool_definition] is unchanged

& [ExactExecution] is one semantic path
  + [embedded_result] is PreparedRuntime ProtocolResponse
  + [resident_result] is the nested ServiceResult ProtocolResponse
  + [structured_content] is the unchanged ProtocolResponse
  + [protocol_fault] retains exact status, exit class, proof, faults, and continuation
  + [service_fault] is a bounded adapter fault with no fabricated semantic result

& [RefreshBehavior] is request-bound and fail closed
  + [MCP_restart] is not required after cantord generation replacement
  + [old_request] produces the exact core response against the new active environment
  + [new_request] succeeds only with supervisor-issued current environment and package bindings
  + [activation] remains outside the model-callable MCP surface

& [ProofSurface] is live
  + [synthetic] is direct core, embedded MCP, service library, resident handler, live cantord, real MCP subprocess, and official MCP client equality
  + [refresh] is old binding failure and new binding success without MCP restart
  + [pinning] is changed config cannot retarget the active client
  + [failure] is bad token startup rejection and post-start service loss adapter fault
  + [rollback] is every prior embedded test remains passing

& [OperatorUse] is explicit
  + [embedded_command] is cantor-mcp --environment absolute_environment_path
  + [resident_command] is cantor-mcp --service-config absolute_service_config_path
  + [Codex] may register either subprocess form through its operator-owned MCP configuration
  - never: register automatically or expose token, refresh, shutdown, or configuration to the model

& [NonclaimSet] is retained
  + [MCP] is STDIO even when its backend uses loopback cantord
  + [service] is local read-only and not remote or multi-user
  + [coordination] is no notification, session, junction, token ring, faculty, or provider inference
  + [semantics] is no adapter-local inference, request repair, or authority minting
